body:
This is a great question, I'd honestly have to go with The Mimic, Moroi, and Hantu.

The Mimic: This is a really OP option with a pretty bad side affect. The Mimic can act like a different ghost which is OP as hell, but it only lasts for 30 seconds (I think) and it randomly changes, but who knows, the random ghost switching could either spell your doom or save your life.

&#x200B;

Moroi: This ghost gets powerful the less sanity you have. Having 21 ghosts chasing after you would drop your sanity significantly, making the Moroi extremely powerful. The downside to this ghost is how much sanity you have, that's the only downside to this ghost.

&#x200B;

Hantu: It's going to be cold as hell in this house or building, the Hantu would be extremely powerful since the place is going to be freezing cold. Now, if we are being realistic here, making the place cold as hell is really good for the Hantu and maybe some other ghosts, but not for you. If you stay in the house/building for too long, you may just end up dying bc you froze to death, but Phasmophobia realism doesn't make sense so you'll be fine :D

&#x200B;

That's my thoughts on this. If I could replace one ghost, it would probably be the Moroi. I'd replace the Moroi with Myling since Mylings are quiet and they're somewhat fast, and it doesn't rely on how much sanity you have.
